# NOITE's pope's punishment (3fpapmal) starts the real INFERNO, which
# survives the 3 minutes: NOITE gets 0x40c (hides), then the time-out's
# 0x40a (5 lives, 500), shows itself, adds 500 and goes to the hall.
#
#   zig-out/bin/noite --headless --scene 3fpapmal --ms 198300 --input tools/play/inferno-3fpapmal-win.input
#   zig-out/bin/noite --headless --scene 3fpapmal --ms 198300 --fix all --input tools/play/inferno-3fpapmal-win.input
#
# The pope's video ends at 15903 (the WinExec); INFERNO starts 1500 ms
# later (17403). The keys are `tools/inferno_plan.py --start 17403`
# (inferno-alone-win.input's game shifted); the time-out is at 197403.
# - Original: INFERNO keeps posting 0x40c after its result (BUGS.md H1):
#   the hall takes them for its TIRO game, hides NOITE and, finding no
#   TIRO window, counts two lost TIRO games (197453, 197503: 3 lives -> 1);
#   then the time-out's repost (H2) is the hall's TIRO win: +500 more and
#   the prison (3fprisao), lives 1, score 1000. A second after the
#   time-out INFERNO spins on WM_DESTROY (H8: the port panics at 198403),
#   hence --ms 198300.
# - `--fix all`: one 0x40c, one 0x40a: the hall, 3 lives, score 500.
